rules.message:
In Next.js 17, implicit fetch caching like `{ cache: 'force-cache' }` is removed in favor of the `'use cache'` directive.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (Next.js 15/16 legacy fetch cache)
const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
  cache: 'force-cache'
});

// ✅ AFTER (Next.js 17 Cache Components)
async function getCachedData() {
  'use cache';
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data');
  return res.json();
}
```
</details>

