rules.message:
`next/router` is deprecated in Next.js 17. Migrate to the App Router using `next/navigation`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (Pages Router)
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';
const router = useRouter();
router.push('/dashboard');

// ✅ AFTER (App Router)
import { useRouter } from 'next/navigation';
const router = useRouter();
router.push('/dashboard');
```
</details>

`next/head` has been removed in Next.js 17. Use the Metadata API instead.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (Pages Router next/head)
import Head from 'next/head';
export default function Page() {
  return <><Head><title>My App</title></Head><h1>Home</h1></>;
}

// ✅ AFTER (App Router Metadata API)
import type { Metadata } from 'next';
export const metadata: Metadata = { title: 'My App' };
export default function Page() { return <h1>Home</h1>; }
```
</details>

Custom `webpack` config in `next.config.js` is unsupported in Next.js 17. Use `turbopack` configuration.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (next.config.js)
module.exports = {
  webpack: (config) => { return config; }
};

// ✅ AFTER (Turbopack configuration)
module.exports = {
  turbopack: {
    rules: {
      '*.svg': { loaders: ['@svgr/webpack'], as: '*.js' }
    }
  }
};
```
</details>

Calling dynamic request APIs synchronously is a hard compile-time failure in Next.js 17. Await `cookies()` and `headers()`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
import { cookies } from 'next/headers';
const token = cookies().get('token');

// ✅ AFTER
import { cookies } from 'next/headers';
const cookieStore = await cookies();
const token = cookieStore.get('token');
```
</details>
